#X obj 645 11 metro.wchoice;
#X obj 230 93 cnv 1 535 252 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 98 The object works like [metro.choice] \, but each period
in the list has its own weight that determines how often it is selected.
Weights can be given as floats or as percentages. The normalized probability
list is available through the read-only property @calc_w \, and the
random generator can be made deterministic by setting @seed to a non-zero
value.;
#X text 240 214 Use case in algorithmic composition: weighted rhythmic
texture. A composer can favour short intervals over long ones by assigning
them higher weights \, for example [50 40% 200 40% 800 20%]. The resulting
pulse is mostly dense but occasionally opens up into longer silences
\, which gives the texture a recognizable statistical character rather
than pure randomness.;
